  "original_proof_step": "Exact finite fixed-chart-cap dyadic Heath–Brown expansion with literal smooth psi(n/R), removal of inactive arithmetic rectangles, and common-functional medium-plus-TypeI assembly. The existing source derives the original 3−3+1 convolution identity and all-slot rough projector; neither is assumed as a new target input.",
  "external_boundary_inputs": [],
  "mathematical_gap_vs_implementation_gap": {
    "original_manuscript": "No new original mathematical gap identified in this finite algebra step. Primitive inputs are positive R, psi(t)=0 for t>2, 2R<=N, 2R<=y^3 and original rough coefficients. The paper supplies y=(2R)^(1/3).",
    "implementation": "New absent module written completely but uncompiled. It uses source-only Oct27 branch API and Oct26 tuple/HB APIs. Dots owns compilation/API repair. Full multi-original-group geometric separation and distribution bounds remain outside this single-group finite identity."
  },
  "deduplication": {
    "existing_exact_HB": "Oct26 P5RealCutoffHeathBrownThree, P5LiteralHeathBrownOccurrenceWords, P5ActualRoughHeathBrownWords, P5ActualHBDyadicOccurrenceFamily reused.",
    "existing_branch_primitives": "Oct27 P5ActualHBMediumBranchPartition, P5ActualHBMediumRoleSupports, P5OriginalHBMediumChartReserves not duplicated.",
    "new_connection": "Old dyadic bank depended on evaluated n. New bank cap N is fixed before n and factor tuples; smooth support discharges cube and n<=N globally, then finite sums are retained and branch partition assembled against common F."
  },
